# Site configuration for SLM Factory: everything that depends on the machine it runs on.
#
#   cp site.env.example site.env      # site.env is git-ignored; edit it for your cluster
#
# Read by scripts/site_env.sh (Slurm launchers and setup scripts) and config/site.py (Python
# entry points). Every key is optional: an unset key falls back to the default in the comment,
# and a variable already set in the environment wins over this file.
# Plain KEY=VALUE lines only (no `export`, no $VAR expansion), so both readers agree.

# --- Caches and scratch (large: keep them off a small home-directory quota) ---------------------
# SLM_CACHE_DIR=<repo>/.cache       parent of the three caches below unless they are set
# UV_CACHE_DIR=<SLM_CACHE_DIR>/uv
# PIP_CACHE_DIR=<SLM_CACHE_DIR>/pip
# HF_HOME=<SLM_CACHE_DIR>/huggingface
# SLM_TMP_DIR=<repo>/.tmp           scratch output of the MNN verification probes and builds

# --- Toolchains ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLAMA_CPP_DIR=<repo>/../llama.cpp llama.cpp checkout (scripts/build_llamacpp_cuda.sh builds it)
# SLM_GCC_LIB=                      GCC >= 12 runtime lib dir (libstdc++ with GLIBCXX_3.4.30) to put
#                                   on .venv_gpu's LD_LIBRARY_PATH when the system one is older

# --- Slurm ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# sbatch reads these itself, so no launcher names an account, partition or QOS. Submit with
# scripts/submit.sh, which loads this file first.
# SBATCH_ACCOUNT=
# SBATCH_PARTITION=
# SBATCH_QOS=
